I had some good luck near the beginning of the game.  There was an
armor store on DL 2 that had studded leather, gloves, and +1 boots of
jumping.  Then, on DL 3, I found a neutral altar that I converted.  I
tried to get Magicbane, but gave up and returned later.  The stairs to
the Mines were on DL 4, and the Oracle was on DL 6.  After I found the
Oracle, I went back to the altar and sacrificed until I got Magicbane.

After I got Magicbane, I went back down and started on Sokoban.  On
the second floor, I was in the back hallway when 3 or 4 winter wolf
cubs came around the corner.  I managed to kill them but I had less
than 10 HP left when I did. I could have easily avoided this, but
there were a few things I forgot about. Near the stairs on the same
level, I found a bag of some type on the ground. I wasn't sure what
type it was, so I just left it and kept going.  On the top level, I
got the bag of holding, and on the way back down, I found that the bag
from level 2 was also a BoH.

Once I had the bag from Sokoban, I went back up and then down into the
mines. There was another BoH on DL 7, and minetown was just below
that, on DL 8.  The temple wasn't coaligned, so I just looked through
the shops for anything useful.  Since I had no light source yet, I
decidedto buy some candles from Izchak's for the rest of the mines.
I used them until i got to Mine's End, where I found a magic lamp.

After I had everything useful from the mines, I went back to the main
dungeon to explore the areas past Sokoban.  On DL 11, I found a
neutral temple, and the Quest portal was on DL 13.  Unfortunately, I
was only XL 12, so I kept going.  There was a leprechaun hall one
level below, and I used the money to buy protection, which lowered my
AC to 1.  Then, I went back to the altar on DL 3 to make some holy
water.  I used it to bless my BoH, unicorn horn, and 2 magic lamps.
Then, I used one of the lamps to wish for a blessd magic marker so I
could write +oID and +oMM.  I used the spell to ID everything and
found that I had a helm of brilliance and a ring of teleport control.
The ring was very useful because I had gotten teleportitis from a
nymph in Sokoban and had been getting teleported randomly for a while.

Nothing interesting happened until DL 21, except finding a hardware
store with a key and a magic whistle on DL 19.  Then, on DL 21, my
telepathy detected a very large throne room with about 30 monsters
inside, including a black dragon. I decided to go lock the door so
they wouldn't start running around the level, but when I tried...
"KABOOM!  The door was booby-trapped!" and all the monsters woke up.
 I engraved Elbereth and dropped gold on 2 squares in the hallway, but
it got eroded, so I ran back upstairs.

I decided to buy some protection (got my AC to -4) and do the Quest
before I tried to get rid of that black dragon.  I got to XL 14 thanks
to a "dishwasher" on DL 9, then went back to the portal on DL 13.
The Quest was pretty easy, and I got poison resistance and teleport
control from some tengus there.  The nemesis was pretty easy to kill,
but I ended up chasing him upstairs several times before I remembered
to teleport to the stairs.  After I did that, I was able to kill him
quickly.  I took the artifacts and headed back to the main dungeon.

After the quest, I came up with an idea for killing the black dragon
on DL 21 with little risk of disintegration.  There was a small
undisturbed throne room on DL 18 that also contained a black dragon.
I used a confused ?oTaming from outside the door to tame everything
inside.  Then, I took the dragon with me down to DL 21 and used a
=oConflict to make the two black dragons fight.  While the hostile one
was busy, I attacked it with magic missiles until it died. Then, I let
the tame dragon protect me while I ate the corpse so it wouldn't rot.
During that time, my pet killed about half the monsters.  I killed
the rest of them and took the black dragon scales, which I used until
the castle.

On DL 22, I found Medusa, and killed her with a mirror.  The Castle
was on DL 25, but a master lich showed up soon after I got there, so I
ran upstairs to rest before killing it.  Then, in the back passageway,
one of the dragons was silver, and it dropped scales when I killed it.
After that, I found the wand.  It came with 3 charges, but I already
had everything I needed for my ascension kit, so I saved them for
later.  I went to the Valley of the Dead so it would appear on the
Eye's teleport menu, then used the Eye to go to Sokoban.  I left
Sokoban then went up to DL 3 to collect my old stash.  I used the Eye
to get back to the castle, then started writing some scrolls with my
old magic marker.  I wrote some charging and enchant armor, then
wished for a cursed magic marker to write cursed destroy armor.  I
used cursed confused destroy armor to fireproof all my armor, then
went back to DL 11 for some more protection before entering Gehennom.

On DL 28, I fell down three levels through a trap door.  I found the
stairs and went up.  A few steps from the stairs... "Juiblex engulfs
you!"  Fortunately, I already had my wand of digging out, so I killed
him quickly and used my unicorn horn to cure myself.  After that, I
went to the stairs and ended up right next to Asmodeus.  I only had
about 200 gold out, so the bribe was pretty cheap.  On DL 34 I found
the stairs to Vlad's, then killed him and took the candelabrum.  I
used the Eye to get back to the Castle, where I stashed all the extra
stuff I had collected and bought some protection before continuing.

I started going down through Gehennom again, and on DL 44 I found the
first fake wizard's tower.  It had the portal, so I went through to
clear out the real tower.  However, there were 4 liches just on the
bottom floor, so I went back to the castle and wrote some genocide
scrolls.  After I had genocided all 'L' and ';' I went back down and
finished clearing out the tower, then went down until I found the
Vibrating Square.  I marked the square and teleported back to the
Castle.  There, I started to polypile some stuff and ended up with 2
"oLS, some good gems, and a book of finger of death.  I also ended up
with detect treasure, which I used to find vaults, including the one
with the portal to Ludios.

After I cleared out Ludios, I decided to use all my money to buy
protection from the priest on DL 11, then kill him and make some
unholy water on his altar.  After I teleported back to the Castle, I
noticed that my AC was much higher than it should have been;
apparently, killing the priest lost me all my protection.  I went to
the priest in the Valley to get most of it back, then enchanted all my
armor to +4 or +5.  This brought my AC to -45.

Once all my armor was enchanted, I decided that I should probably have
more than 94 HP for the ascension run.  I wrote a c?oGeno and
teleported to Sokoban. I reverse-genocided nurses, and in less than
600 turns, I had more than doubled my HP.  Afterwards, I went to DL 3
to try sacrificing for a decent artifact weapon, but I only got two
useless ones.  However, praying did boost my HP by 15 or 20 points,
putting it a bit over 200.

I decided that I should head back to the Castle and get everything set
up for the ascension run.  I wrote some blessed and cursed genocide
scrolls and did some alchemy for some blessed ?oFH.  I also decided to
try wishing for Frost Brand, and ended up getting it on the first try.

Once everything was ready, I used a few c?oTele to go straight to the
portal to the tower, then from the tower to the Vibrating Square.  The
sanctum was not too difficult, and I found another "oLS in one of the
chests in the graveyard. Then, I used my magic whistle to get my pet
purple worm, black dragon, and white dragon into the left area without
even opening the door.  They killed most of the stuff there, and I got
the rest with finger of death.  I put all my flammable stuff into the
bag, then searched for the door to the temple.  I smashed it, then
killed the priest with finger of death and took the amulet.

The way out of Gehennom wasn't very difficult, and the mysterious
force didn't bother me too much.  The Wizard only showed up one time
between the Sanctum and the Planes.  At the Castle, I grabbed my wands
of death (I had forgotten them) and kept going.  I finally made it to
DL 1, and was ready for the Planes.

On the Plane of Earth, I killed the wizard and the minotaur and
grabbed the extra wand of digging.  I used my wands to dig around most
of the elementals, but I did have to kill the Wizard when he showed up
a second time.  Confused gold detection had shown the portal to be in
the farthest cavern from the entrance, but I made it there without too
much trouble.  For some reason, my pets wouldn't go through the
portal, so I had to leave my black and white dragons and woodchuck
(large cat + doppelganger corpse).  I made it to the Plane of Air and
somehow managed to avoid the elementals and vortices.  For some
reason, my pets would now activate the portal when they stepped on it.
I sent my large cat and purple worm through, then followed them to the
Plane of Fire.  Here, I used confused ?oGD to find the fire traps, and
just ran around them.  However, when I got to the portal and summoned
my pets, the purple worm wouldn't move off the portal or activate it,
so I tried to displace it to the side.  I ended up pushing it into
lava, which is why Anhur was angry at the end of the game.  I did
manage to take my large cat with me to the Plane of Water, but it was
soon killed by 2 cobras.  Cursed ?oGD let me see the portal, and I
just waited and killed elementals until it appeared.  I jumped through
and appeared on the Astral Plane.

As soon as I arrived, I used telepathy and found Death to the left,
Famine in the middle, and Pestilence to the right.  Also, Famine had
unlocked and opened his door and monsters were starting to come out.
I ran over and used confused create monster to try to block the door,
but the blobs kept moving.  I used two more scrolls and ran over to
the right.  Since I had a short break, I decided to blessed-genocide
'a' and 'S' to block summon insects/sticks to snakes.  Then, I
reverse-genocided and tamed 6 purple worms, opened the door, and stood
to the side helping kill whatever was in the doorway.  I took care of
most of the monsters in the round room, then moved on to the temple
courtyard.  Before I even got all the way into the courtyard, I got
this message: "You feel aggravated at the invisible high priest of
Ptah!"  Since I now knew that this was the wrong temple, I ran back
out and blocked the way with an acid blob between 2 burned Elbereths.
I headed to the middle room because I didn't want to fight Death, and
started zapping everything with my /oTele.  I finally had a clear path
to the altar, and found it was chaotic!

(About the high priest and his cursed !oInvis: Is this a bug?
Wizard-mode testing shows that the alignment of a high temple can
normally only be determined by actually standing on the altar.)

